    seoTitle: "Doug Ford Directs $420M for Bradford Bypass Eco-Bridges | Choseno",
    metaDescription: "Ontario Premier Doug Ford awards $420M to build 3 vegetated wildlife eco-bridges and wetland causeways on the Bradford Bypass.",
    tweet: "Premier Doug Ford awards $420M to construct three vegetated wildlife eco-bridges and wetland causeways along the Bradford Bypass.",
    tweetarticle: "Ontario Premier Doug Ford and Transportation Minister Prabmeet Sarkaria have awarded a $420 million design-build contract to construct three vegetated wildlife eco-bridges and elevated wetland causeways along the 16-kilometer Bradford Bypass highway corridor connecting Highway 400 to Highway 404.\n\nReview Doug Ford on Choseno:\nhttps://choseno.com/wall/doug-ford\n\nWHAT CHANGED & TAXPAYER IMPACT:\n- Directs $420M from the Ontario Building Transportation Infrastructure Fund.\n- Constructs 3 heavily landscaped wildlife eco-bridges spanning 4 highway lanes in the Holland Marsh watershed.\n- Builds 4.2 kilometers of elevated concrete causeway over sensitive wetland terrain, preserving natural groundwater flows.\n- Installs automated acoustic animal-detection warning signs and continuous wildlife exclusion fencing.\n\nTHE DEBATE:\n- Provincial Government & Simcoe County Commuters: Highlight that the bypass cuts 35 minutes off East-West travel times for freight and commuters while specialized eco-bridges safeguard local deer, moose, and turtle populations.\n- Environmental Watchdogs & Farmland Alliances: Acknowledge the wildlife bridges while maintaining concerns over long-term highway runoff impacts on the Holland Marsh specialty agricultural crop basin.\n\nNOW YOU HAVE THE SAY — CHOSENO:\nChoseno is like Google Reviews for politicians. Don't just watch decisions happen from the sidelines — now you have the say. Review Doug Ford's record, speak your mind, and let your fellow constituents know where you stand on his official public wall:\nhttps://choseno.com/wall/doug-ford\n\nRead the full investigative report on Choseno:\nhttps://choseno.com/news/premier-doug-ford-awards-420-million-for-bradford-bypass-wetland-eco-bridges-and-wildlife-fencing-2026-08-25\n\n#Ontario #DougFord #PrabmeetSarkaria #BradfordBypass #ONPoli #Infrastructure #Transportation #Choseno",
    breakingNews: false,
    body: "BRADFORD, Ont. — Premier Doug Ford and Minister of Transportation Prabmeet Sarkaria announced on Monday the awarding of a $420 million infrastructure contract to construct three specialized vegetated wildlife eco-bridges, elevated roadway causeways, and subterranean amphibian tunnels along the planned 16.2-kilometer Bradford Bypass corridor connecting Highway 400 in Simcoe County to Highway 404 in York Region.\n\nThe project incorporates comprehensive environmental mitigation architecture into the four-lane highway design, addressing environmental concerns regarding habitat fragmentation across the Holland River wetland ecosystem while alleviating severe regional gridlock on local municipal roads.\n\nEcological Engineering for the Holland Marsh Corridor\nThe $420 million contract finances:\n- 3 Vegetated Wildlife Eco-Bridges: Engineered overpasses featuring native coniferous tree canopies, thick brush plantings, and acoustic sound barriers designed to facilitate safe crossings for large mammals and local wildlife.\n- 4.2 Kilometers of Elevated Wetland Causeway: Replacing standard earthen highway berms with elevated bridge pilings to maintain natural groundwater movement through the Holland River floodplain.\n- 28 Subterranean Micro-Culverts & Exclusion Fencing: Specialized climate-controlled tunnels designed specifically for Blanding's turtles, salamanders, and small mammals.\n\n\"Our government is getting it done for drivers across York Region and Simcoe County by building the Bradford Bypass, cutting down on gridlock, and keeping goods moving across our economy,\" Premier Doug Ford said during an announcement in Bradford. \"By investing $420 million in world-class wildlife overpasses and elevated wetland causeways, we are protecting our natural environment, safeguarding local wildlife, and building a modern highway that serves generations of Ontarians.\"\n\nRegional mayors, building trades unions, and trucking industry executives commended the contract award, pointing out that connecting Highway 400 to Highway 404 saves commercial transport carriers over 35 minutes per trip and removes thousands of heavy freight trucks from local downtown streets in Bradford and East Gwillimbury."
