    summary: "Alberta Premier Danielle Smith and Agriculture Minister RJ Sigurdson allocate $220 million to convert 200 kilometers of open earthen irrigation canals into pressurized subterranean underground pipelines, conserving 150 million cubic meters of agricultural water in Southern Alberta.",
